<main id="main" class="page spec-body">
  <h1>Start: build a todo app</h1>

  <p>This is the one walkthrough this site maintains by hand, and it is kept honest mechanically: every code sample below also lives in <a href="https://github.com/waaseyaa/waaseyaa-org/blob/main/tests/Tutorial/TodoAppTest.php">this site's test suite</a>, which runs against the exact framework version serving this page ({{ framework_version }}). If the framework changes under the tutorial, the tests break and this page changes with them. Everything deeper than the walkthrough lives in the <a href="/docs">spec corpus</a>, which is published from the framework repository with provenance and cannot go stale by construction.</p>

  <p>Waaseyaa is alpha software; APIs still move between releases. The <a href="/docs/specs/stability-charter">stability charter</a> says which surfaces are protected.</p>

  <h2>1. Install</h2>

  <pre><code>composer create-project waaseyaa/waaseyaa my-app --stability=dev
cd my-app
./vendor/bin/waaseyaa db:init
./vendor/bin/waaseyaa serve</code></pre>

  <p>The <code>--stability=dev</code> flag is required during the alpha. <code>db:init</code> creates the SQLite database and applies migrations; it is idempotent and safe to run on every deploy. The dev server answers at <code>http://localhost:8080</code>.</p>

  <h2>2. Define the entity</h2>

  <p>One PHP class is one kind of thing your application stores. The class declares everything about itself with attributes: <code>#[ContentEntityType]</code> names the type (and opts into JSON:API with <code>api: true</code>), <code>#[ContentEntityKeys]</code> maps logical keys to fields, and each <code>#[Field]</code> marks a public typed property as a persistable field. Field types are inferred from the PHP property types.</p>

  <p>Every field also declares who may read it. Waaseyaa is deny-by-default at the field level too: a field without a read level is internal and application code cannot read it. That is a deliberate property of the framework, not a tutorial inconvenience; see <a href="/docs/specs/field-access">field-access.md</a>.</p>

  <p>Create <code>src/Entity/Todo.php</code>:</p>

  <pre><code>&lt;?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Entity;

use Waaseyaa\Entity\Attribute\ContentEntityKeys;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\Attribute\ContentEntityType;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\Attribute\Field;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\ContentEntityBase;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\FieldReadLevel;

#[ContentEntityType(id: 'todo', label: 'Todo', api: true)]
#[ContentEntityKeys(label: 'title')]
class Todo extends ContentEntityBase
{
    #[Field(label: 'Title', required: true, read: FieldReadLevel::Public)]
    public string $title = '';

    #[Field(label: 'Completed', read: FieldReadLevel::Public)]
    public bool $completed = false;

    #[Field(label: 'Priority', read: FieldReadLevel::Public)]
    public string $priority = 'normal';

    public function isCompleted(): bool
    {
        return (bool) $this->get('completed');
    }

    public function toggleCompleted(): static
    {
        return $this->set('completed', !$this->isCompleted());
    }
}</code></pre>

  <p>Register it in <code>config/entity-types.php</code>. Because the class carries its own metadata, registration is one line:</p>

  <pre><code>&lt;?php

declare(strict_types=1);

use Waaseyaa\Entity\EntityType;

return [
    EntityType::fromClass(\App\Entity\Todo::class),
];</code></pre>

  <p>Then create the table and rebuild the compiled manifest:</p>

  <pre><code>./vendor/bin/waaseyaa schema:sync
./vendor/bin/waaseyaa optimize:manifest</code></pre>

  <h2>3. Routes and a typed controller</h2>

  <p>A service provider registers routes. <code>entityParameter('todo', 'todo')</code> marks <code>{todo}</code> as an entity segment: the framework loads the row and passes a <code>Todo</code> instance into any action parameter typed as <code>Todo</code>. Unknown ids become a 404 before your code runs. <code>allowAll()</code> and <code>csrfExempt()</code> are tutorial settings; routes are deny-by-default and real applications use permissions and CSRF, per <a href="/docs/specs/access-control">access-control.md</a>.</p>

  <p>Create <code>src/Provider/TodoServiceProvider.php</code>:</p>

  <pre><code>&lt;?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Provider;

use Waaseyaa\Foundation\ServiceProvider\ServiceProvider;
use Waaseyaa\Routing\RouteBuilder;
use Waaseyaa\Routing\WaaseyaaRouter;

class TodoServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
{
    public function routes(
        WaaseyaaRouter $router,
        ?\Waaseyaa\Entity\EntityTypeManager $entityTypeManager = null,
    ): void {
        $router->addRoute('todo.list', RouteBuilder::create('/todos')
            ->controller('App\Controller\TodoController::list')
            ->methods('GET')
            ->allowAll()
            ->build());

        $router->addRoute('todo.create', RouteBuilder::create('/todos')
            ->controller('App\Controller\TodoController::create')
            ->methods('POST')
            ->allowAll()
            ->csrfExempt()
            ->build());

        $router->addRoute('todo.toggle', RouteBuilder::create('/todos/{todo}/toggle')
            ->controller('App\Controller\TodoController::toggle')
            ->entityParameter('todo', 'todo')
            ->methods('POST')
            ->allowAll()
            ->csrfExempt()
            ->build());

        $router->addRoute('todo.delete', RouteBuilder::create('/todos/{todo}/delete')
            ->controller('App\Controller\TodoController::delete')
            ->entityParameter('todo', 'todo')
            ->methods('POST')
            ->allowAll()
            ->csrfExempt()
            ->build());
    }
}</code></pre>

  <p>Add the provider class to <code>extra.waaseyaa.providers</code> in <code>composer.json</code>, next to the default entry, and run <code>./vendor/bin/waaseyaa optimize:manifest</code> again.</p>

  <p>Persistence goes through the entity repository: <code>create()</code> builds a new, unsaved entity with defaults applied, <code>save()</code> inserts or updates, <code>find()</code> loads by id, <code>findBy([])</code> returns everything, <code>delete()</code> removes one entity. Create <code>src/Controller/TodoController.php</code>:</p>

  <pre><code>&lt;?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Controller;

use App\Entity\Todo;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\RedirectResponse;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Request;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Response;
use Twig\Environment;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\EntityTypeManagerInterface;

final class TodoController
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly EntityTypeManagerInterface $entityTypeManager,
        private readonly Environment $twig,
    ) {}

    public function list(): Response
    {
        $repository = $this->entityTypeManager->getRepository('todo');
        $todos = $repository->findBy([]);

        $html = $this->twig->render('todo/list.html.twig', [
            'todos' => $todos,
            'pending' => array_values(array_filter($todos, fn (Todo $t) => !$t->isCompleted())),
            'completed' => array_values(array_filter($todos, fn (Todo $t) => $t->isCompleted())),
        ]);

        return new Response($html);
    }

    public function create(Request $request): Response
    {
        $title = trim((string) $request->request->get('title', ''));
        if ($title === '') {
            return new RedirectResponse('/todos');
        }

        $repository = $this->entityTypeManager->getRepository('todo');
        $todo = $repository->create([
            'title' => $title,
            'completed' => false,
            'priority' => $request->request->get('priority', 'normal'),
        ]);
        $repository->save($todo);

        return new RedirectResponse('/todos');
    }

    public function toggle(Todo $todo): Response
    {
        $todo->toggleCompleted();
        $this->entityTypeManager->getRepository('todo')->save($todo);

        return new RedirectResponse('/todos');
    }

    public function delete(Todo $todo): Response
    {
        $this->entityTypeManager->getRepository('todo')->delete($todo);

        return new RedirectResponse('/todos');
    }
}</code></pre>

  <p>The HTML lives in Twig, not in the controller. A minimal <code>templates/todo/list.html.twig</code> is a form posting to <code>/todos</code> plus two loops over <code>pending</code> and <code>completed</code>; the shape is yours to choose.</p>

  <h2>4. Run it</h2>

  <pre><code>./vendor/bin/waaseyaa serve</code></pre>

  <p>Open <code>http://localhost:8080/todos</code>. Add a few todos, toggle them, delete one. That is the whole loop: entity, registration, routes, controller, template.</p>

  <h2>5. The API you already have</h2>

  <p>Because the class declared <code>api: true</code>, the same type is served over JSON:API at <code>/api/todo</code>. Entity access still applies there: JSON:API runs view and create checks per entity, and with no access policy the collection is empty. That asymmetry is intentional; the web routes above said <code>allowAll()</code>, the API makes you say who may see what. Add a policy when you want the API open, per <a href="/docs/specs/access-control">access-control.md</a> and <a href="/docs/specs/jsonapi">jsonapi.md</a>.</p>

